======================================================================================================================================================
INTERPRETATION GUARDRAILS
======================================================================================================================================================

1. delta_L is the observed Vanilla-vs-SEASC representation displacement.
2. u_L is the direct actuator applied at layer L.
3. u_L != delta_L in general because earlier interventions are transported
   through subsequent transformer blocks.
4. cos(delta_L, A_L) tells whether the observed displacement points toward
   the CURRENT layer's extracted SEASC actuator direction.
5. PCA is only a 2D visualization. Exact distances and angles are computed
   in the full hidden-dimensional space.
6. Large coordinate changes do NOT by themselves identify individual
   'concept neurons'.
7. Output change does NOT imply increased intelligence or improved factual
   correctness.
8. TEST142 is a mechanistic X-ray of the existing frozen SEASC 3.0 motor;
   it does not alter the compass, DRA envelope, or controller architecture.

